From: shphadnis <134159681+shphadnis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:18:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] spectro: fix Nutanix re-review findings in ConfigMaps and
 inventory

- Label the libvirt domain-XML ConfigMap resource=vm-domain-xml instead
  of inheriting vm-config from vmLabels. ensureConfigMap selects the CDI
  cert ConfigMap by vmLabels and takes the first match, so a leftover
  domain-XML ConfigMap could be handed to CDI as certConfigMap, which
  has no ca.pem and fails a secure Prism import.
- Return storage container listing errors from the Nutanix collector.
  The error was logged and dropped, which marked the provider ready with
  no storage inventory; plan validation then reported the disks as
  unmapped instead of the inventory failure.

Resolves: None

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
